This directory contains an unmodified subset of STMicroelectronics STM32CubeH7
v1.12.1 and its pinned HAL/CMSIS Device submodules, plus ARM CMSIS headers shipped
by that release. The complete upstream repository is not required to build the
teaching example. CMake uses only the files in this directory and the local
application; it does not download dependencies.

SOURCES.json records each original repository, commit, source path, Git blob ID
and SHA256. The Cube commit is f5c0b7a2b1f6eb26fde150f72edb2d7deb647066;
its HAL and CMSIS Device gitlinks are verified in that commit's Git trees.

HAL/LICENSE.txt contains the original HAL BSD 3-Clause license.
CMSIS/Device/LICENSE.txt contains the original CMSIS Device Apache-2.0 license.
CMSIS/Core/LICENSE.txt contains the original ARM CMSIS Apache-2.0 license.
STM32CubeH7-LICENSE.txt contains the original Cube package license notice.
reference/LICENSE.txt contains the original NUCLEO-H723ZG Templates BSD 3-Clause
license, including the linker script's license.
These license files retain the original bytes; only their local filenames differ.
All copyright and license notices in the source files are retained.

reference/STM32H723ZGTX_FLASH.ld is the original NUCLEO-H723ZG GCC linker template.
The teaching target uses it unchanged: 1 MiB Flash, 128 KiB DTCM RAM and the
official reset/startup symbols. The application selects HSI64 and LDO through
the public HAL and uses the official SystemInit, startup vector and SysTick API.
